WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:03.330
Take care now!

00:03.330 --> 00:04.810
You, too!

00:05.070 --> 00:08.150
He was so hospitable.

00:09.740 --> 00:11.270
What's wrong?

00:11.270 --> 00:14.110
I just hope Keithwood 
and the others are okay.

00:14.110 --> 00:17.610
<i>I see even Sion has a human side to him.</i>

00:17.610 --> 00:19.770
<i>That's a bit surprising.</i>

00:19.770 --> 00:21.810
If that group attacked again,

00:21.810 --> 00:24.330
it'd be pretty tough for 
me to handle alone, so...

00:24.780 --> 00:31.010
Um, when you say it'd be tough, 
what do you mean by that?

00:31.010 --> 00:34.640
I've never slain a person 
on the battlefield before.

00:34.640 --> 00:36.550
That battle was my first.

00:36.550 --> 00:37.390
Huh?

00:38.030 --> 00:39.550
Of course, I'll do my best,

00:40.060 --> 00:42.640
but unfortunately, I can't 
guarantee your safety.

00:44.030 --> 00:48.020
<i>Mr. Keithwood, please be okay!</i>

02:18.700 --> 02:23.200
I had heard there is an atmosphere 
of unrest in the Kingdom of Remno,

02:23.430 --> 02:26.000
but I didn't expect Princess 
Mia to be heading there.

02:23.700 --> 02:29.750
<b>Episode 10: Princess Miya Is Kidnapped!</b>

02:26.000 --> 02:27.120
Yes...

02:27.120 --> 02:30.460
I would normally want to dispatch 
the Princess Guard, but...

02:31.340 --> 02:35.030
In these circumstances, any troop movements 
could be viewed as a potential invasion.

02:35.300 --> 02:36.570
Mr. Dion!

02:36.570 --> 02:40.260
I swear, our princess always 
does such amusing things.

02:40.510 --> 02:42.250
This is no laughing matter.

02:42.250 --> 02:44.360
If something were to 
happen to Princess Mia...

02:44.360 --> 02:45.500
No need to worry.

02:45.500 --> 02:48.730
If the sword prodigy Prince Sion 
is with her, she should be fine.

02:48.730 --> 02:50.560
That may be so,

02:50.560 --> 02:53.840
but Remno isn't in a situation 
where a revolution would occur.

02:53.840 --> 02:55.440
What do you mean?

02:55.880 --> 02:59.300
The tax increase has caused a rise 
in discontent among the populace,

02:59.300 --> 03:02.410
but such dramatic backlash should 
not be happening this quickly.

03:02.410 --> 03:04.040
So then...

03:04.040 --> 03:07.330
Are you saying that someone is 
deliberately trying to incite revolution?

03:07.330 --> 03:09.860
How awful! Who would do that?

03:10.140 --> 03:13.460
Whatever the case, we need to 
stop it before there's bloodshed.

03:13.990 --> 03:17.960
But solving the matter 
without a single casualty

03:17.960 --> 03:20.260
seems like a tall order, 
even for the princess.

03:20.260 --> 03:24.480
Even so, if anyone can do it, Princess Mia can.

03:25.490 --> 03:29.200
I must say, this area seems quite peaceful.

03:29.200 --> 03:31.710
In these parts, we don't even have bandits,

03:31.710 --> 03:34.750
so it's a very easy place 
for us to do business.

03:34.750 --> 03:37.010
But there <i>is</i> a civil war going on.

03:37.280 --> 03:39.780
That doesn't have much 
to do with us out here.

03:39.780 --> 03:43.910
I did hear that there was a 
revolt in Count Donovan's lands.

03:43.910 --> 03:48.870
Word is they deployed the 
Adamant Infantry to quell the rebellion.

03:49.230 --> 03:51.100
The Adamant Infantry?

03:51.100 --> 03:53.500
That'll result in a unilateral massacre.

03:53.500 --> 03:56.260
What's the Adamant Infantry?

03:56.260 --> 03:59.700
They're an elite force formed directly 
by the King of Remno.

03:59.700 --> 04:04.970
A heavily armored force comprised entirely
 of soldiers with the prowess of 1,000 fighters.

04:05.290 --> 04:07.920
<i>They sound incredibly strong!</i>

04:07.920 --> 04:12.020
<i>Maybe I can scout a few for my guards?</i>

04:12.020 --> 04:14.980
<i>Even if they're a revolutionary army,
 they're still the kingdom's people.</i>

04:15.360 --> 04:16.910
<i>The revolutionaries are citizens.</i>

04:16.910 --> 04:19.450
<i>To send such a mighty 
force to suppress them...</i>

04:20.110 --> 04:23.140
So then, how great have the losses been?

04:23.580 --> 04:26.460
From what I hear, it seems like 
there haven't been any yet.

04:26.460 --> 04:27.370
What?

04:27.700 --> 04:30.760
They supposedly haven't clashed 
in battle even once yet.

04:30.760 --> 04:34.050
Those soldiers are as valuable
 as diamonds after all.

04:36.960 --> 04:40.960
Drat! I can't see anything 
but a silly love letter here!

04:40.960 --> 04:42.800
<i>This man is Graham.</i>

04:42.800 --> 04:47.080
<i>He is a member of Sunkland's 
intelligence agency, the Wind Crows,</i>

04:47.080 --> 04:51.600
<i>and right now, he is operating within the 
Remno government as a civil servant.</i>

04:51.890 --> 04:54.220
<i>Prince Abel, I do hope this 
letter finds you well.</i>

04:55.840 --> 04:58.280
No! There must be more here!

04:58.280 --> 05:01.820
She must be employing some method 
to communicate with Prince Abel!

05:02.350 --> 05:05.220
The plan to plunge Remno 
into a revolutionary war

05:05.220 --> 05:10.270
was originally supposed to begin after 
the fall of the Tearmoon Empire.

05:10.810 --> 05:14.120
It's all because of that damn girl Mia!

05:16.200 --> 05:17.960
Excuse me, sir.

05:18.250 --> 05:19.440
Monica.

05:19.440 --> 05:23.010
Sir, I believe you may be 
speaking a bit too loudly.

05:23.010 --> 05:25.100
So, why are you here?

05:25.100 --> 05:26.330
I have a report.

05:26.620 --> 05:31.500
It's about Princess Mia and Prince Sion's 
attempt to cross the border.

05:31.500 --> 05:33.310
It would appear that they have escaped.

05:33.970 --> 05:38.790
We are attempting to locate their companions,
 but their whereabouts are unknown.

05:41.110 --> 05:44.220
You don't think they anticipated 
the attack, do you?

05:44.220 --> 05:47.640
Were Princess Mia and Prince Abel
 in communication after all?

05:48.330 --> 05:52.460
This appears to simply be a typical 
exchange between a boy and girl their age.

05:52.460 --> 05:53.420
It can't be!

05:53.420 --> 05:57.650
If it were, he wouldn't have sent 
her horse shampoo as a present!

05:58.070 --> 06:00.950
That had to be some sort of code!

06:00.950 --> 06:03.170
Like, "Ready a swift horse," or something.

06:03.170 --> 06:05.130
Might you be reading too far into it?

06:05.130 --> 06:07.280
<i>He is indeed reading too far into it.</i>

06:07.280 --> 06:11.470
Whatever the case, our maneuvers to 
destroy the Tearmoon Empire ended in failure.

06:11.470 --> 06:15.140
We'll have to accelerate our plans, 
even if it means taking some risks.

06:15.140 --> 06:16.960
Isn't everything proceeding smoothly so far?

06:17.250 --> 06:18.810
We're walking a tightrope.

06:19.100 --> 06:23.320
We spread word that the king 
confined Count Donovan,

06:23.320 --> 06:27.850
thus inciting a revolt by stirring up 
those unhappy with the royal government.

06:28.110 --> 06:31.620
As a result, the rebel forces gained 
control of the major city facilities.

06:31.620 --> 06:35.970
Then just as we'd hoped, the 
king deployed the Adamant Infantry.

06:35.970 --> 06:40.930
When a massacre occurs, the flames of 
rebellion will spread across the kingdom.

06:40.930 --> 06:42.550
That's how it's supposed to go, anyway.

06:43.090 --> 06:44.670
Is there some problem?

06:44.670 --> 06:48.120
There has been no movement from
 the lynchpin, the Adamant Infantry!

06:48.460 --> 06:50.330
Why are they dawdling out there?

06:50.330 --> 06:53.430
Captain Goliar, why do you not attack?

06:53.430 --> 06:56.870
I cannot keep those ruffians 
in check any longer!

06:56.870 --> 07:02.580
I know. Putting down an essentially 
amateur rebel army is a simple task.

07:02.580 --> 07:04.190
But for now, just wait.

07:04.190 --> 07:04.950
Yes, sir.

07:07.460 --> 07:10.360
Goliar, as you know,

07:10.360 --> 07:16.390
the Adamant Infantry is my prized 
elite force formed over the past ten years.

07:16.390 --> 07:18.230
It is an honor, Your Majesty.

07:18.230 --> 07:20.360
Therefore, on your first battle,

07:20.360 --> 07:24.210
deliver a superb victory without 
losing a single soldier.

07:24.480 --> 07:25.490
Yes, Your Majesty—

07:25.490 --> 07:26.510
Your Majesty?

07:26.510 --> 07:28.910
Without losing a single soldier?

07:28.910 --> 07:35.840
I mustn't lose one of my precious soldiers 
over a mere provincial uprising.

07:36.530 --> 07:39.920
<i>Wipe out the enemy without losing a soldier?</i>

07:40.420 --> 07:42.670
How on earth do I do that?

07:42.670 --> 07:45.690
<i>The sad plight of middle management.</i>

07:46.210 --> 07:49.680
Could this, too, be one of the 
Wisdom of the Empire's schemes?

07:49.680 --> 07:51.190
What would you like me to do?

07:52.490 --> 07:54.560
Send this message home.

07:54.560 --> 07:56.120
Excuse me, sir.

07:58.160 --> 08:02.650
This is... false information that would 
drag our nation into the horrors of war.

08:03.030 --> 08:05.360
Is it really all right to send this?

08:05.360 --> 08:08.910
That's the concern appropriate 
for you black crows.

08:08.910 --> 08:13.470
Do your utmost not to stand out and 
just collect information in secret.

08:15.080 --> 08:18.530
But I'm a white crow, an Albus.

08:18.530 --> 08:24.310
My ambition is to use information as a 
weapon to fight for the glory of Sunkland.

08:24.310 --> 08:28.700
<i>A special force a certain man 
created within the Wind Crows,</i>

08:28.700 --> 08:31.530
<i>Albus, the group 
to which Graham belongs.</i>

08:31.530 --> 08:33.160
You are well aware, aren't you?

08:33.160 --> 08:37.100
Albus missions take priority over all others.

08:37.100 --> 08:38.020
Yes, sir.

08:41.230 --> 08:44.430
<i>King Sunkland prizes justice and fairness.</i>

08:44.430 --> 08:49.240
<i>To get to work for such a man 
was something I was proud of...</i>

08:52.710 --> 08:56.080
Watch where you're going. What a nuisance.

08:56.520 --> 08:57.830
I'm very sorry.

08:59.710 --> 09:03.170
Do you think the apology of 
a lowly maid makes up for it?

09:04.750 --> 09:07.770
<i>This sort of thing is an everyday 
occurrence in this country.</i>

09:08.110 --> 09:09.720
<i>It's better that we...</i>

09:10.480 --> 09:11.670
Pick those up.

09:11.670 --> 09:12.430
Huh?

09:16.390 --> 09:19.150
O-Oh, Your Highness Prince Abel.

09:19.150 --> 09:22.230
I, uh, you see, she...

09:22.610 --> 09:24.900
I believe I told you to pick those up.

09:24.240 --> 09:25.360
Y-Yes, Your Highness.

09:29.420 --> 09:32.870
Should you commit an affront 
against a maid again,

09:32.870 --> 09:33.840
there will be no mercy.

09:33.840 --> 09:37.110
Y-Yes, Your Highness! I will be on my way.

09:37.110 --> 09:39.200
I beg your pardon, Your Highness.

09:39.200 --> 09:41.680
No, I'm sorry you had to go through that.

09:41.680 --> 09:44.520
I'm sure it makes it tough 
for you all to work.

09:45.100 --> 09:50.040
Um, you may interpret this 
as rude of me to say, but...

09:51.310 --> 09:52.810
You've changed, Your Highness.

09:52.810 --> 09:54.530
Oh? Have I?

09:54.530 --> 09:57.100
Yes. You're stronger and more resolute.

09:58.110 --> 10:01.310
Well, I can't let her see me being pathetic.

10:01.310 --> 10:04.190
<i>"Her"... the Wisdom of the Empire,</i>

10:04.190 --> 10:07.380
<i>the girl who turned Prince Abel 
into a brave young lion.</i>

10:08.000 --> 10:11.030
What kind of person is 
this lady you speak of?

10:11.650 --> 10:15.730
She's completely out of 
my league as I am now...

10:16.520 --> 10:21.640
But she believed in me and encouraged me, 
told me I could be more than I am now.

10:22.730 --> 10:26.420
So I need to live up to the 
faith she's placed in me.

10:26.420 --> 10:27.600
I need to work harder.

10:28.370 --> 10:29.550
At least, that's how I felt...

10:30.090 --> 10:32.800
Are you... going to the front, Your Highness?

10:33.090 --> 10:36.070
It appears the battle is at a standstill.

10:36.070 --> 10:39.330
It's been decided that
 I'll join to rouse the troops.

10:39.920 --> 10:42.980
I intend to fulfill my 
royal duties as prince.

10:43.410 --> 10:45.320
Is there something weighing on you?

10:45.320 --> 10:47.930
Oh, no. It's nothing.

10:48.550 --> 10:49.400
It's just...

10:50.250 --> 10:55.420
I'm sure she won't forgive me for 
participating in the suppression of the people.

11:04.320 --> 11:06.070
Take this to the homeland.

11:16.820 --> 11:19.640
<i>I wrote the truth in this one.</i>

11:20.000 --> 11:23.100
<i>There's no guarantee this will reach him.</i>

11:25.810 --> 11:26.750
But...

11:27.940 --> 11:29.330
I pray it does.

11:33.730 --> 11:36.450
So what do we do now?

11:36.450 --> 11:39.240
For now, I'd like to 
rendezvous with Keithwood.

11:39.240 --> 11:40.340
Rendezvous?

11:40.720 --> 11:43.720
We selected a rendezvous point ahead 
of time in case we got separated.

11:43.720 --> 11:46.080
It's apparently about half a 
day's carriage ride from here.

11:46.080 --> 11:48.560
But where will we find a carriage?

11:48.560 --> 11:53.090
That merchant said there's a
 regularly scheduled carriage...

11:54.500 --> 11:55.980
Ah, there it is.

11:55.980 --> 11:57.310
But...

11:58.180 --> 12:02.030
Oh, my, Sion. Do you perhaps 
have no money on hand?

12:02.270 --> 12:05.300
I left all the money with Keithwood.

12:05.300 --> 12:07.870
Then there's no other choice.

12:08.900 --> 12:10.330
Wh-What are you doing?

12:10.570 --> 12:12.900
I made preparations for an emergency.

12:14.130 --> 12:15.880
Why do you keep it there?

12:15.880 --> 12:19.620
Why, so it isn't easy to steal, of course!

12:19.620 --> 12:21.590
<i>In the prior timeline...</i>

12:22.460 --> 12:25.330
<i>Mia had a terrible experience.</i>

12:25.330 --> 12:29.040
I-I don't have anything else! Truly!

12:29.370 --> 12:31.770
Liar! Do a little jump for us.

12:34.520 --> 12:35.480
Huh?

12:35.890 --> 12:37.180
I heard coins jingling.

12:37.180 --> 12:39.000
You've still got more on you!

12:39.670 --> 12:42.830
I won't make that same mistake again.

12:42.830 --> 12:46.850
I gathered currency from the 
neighboring nations ahead of time

12:46.850 --> 12:49.740
so I can always be ready 
to make a smooth escape!

12:50.550 --> 12:53.040
Is this enough to let us ride the carriage?

12:53.040 --> 12:55.360
Very like you to be so well prepared.

12:55.360 --> 12:57.090
With that much, I think we...

12:59.400 --> 13:03.050
<i>How much does a 
stagecoach ride cost exactly?</i>

13:03.430 --> 13:06.320
<i>Naturally, both are sheltered 
from such mundane things.</i>

13:06.320 --> 13:09.510
C-Can I leave the negotiations to you?

13:09.510 --> 13:11.000
O-Of course.

13:11.380 --> 13:16.730
It wouldn't do to make a lady 
pay and then do nothing myself.

13:17.000 --> 13:20.880
Be careful not to let them 
take advantage of you!

13:21.500 --> 13:22.780
I know. I won't.

13:23.670 --> 13:27.530
So even a perfect superhuman 
like him has stuff he's bad at.

13:32.480 --> 13:33.590
Mia!

13:43.180 --> 13:44.130
Huh?

13:45.370 --> 13:46.790
Wh-Where am I?

13:46.790 --> 13:48.830
Oh, you're awake?

13:48.830 --> 13:51.040
<i>What if it's them?</i>

13:53.700 --> 13:56.640
<i>It doesn't really look like it...</i>

13:56.640 --> 14:01.300
Let's get right to it. Got any money on you?

14:01.300 --> 14:02.260
What?

14:02.560 --> 14:05.390
Gold, silver, accessories, and whatnot.

14:05.390 --> 14:07.330
I don't have anything!

14:07.330 --> 14:08.600
Really?

14:09.120 --> 14:11.480
Then why don't you hop up and down a bit.

14:13.390 --> 14:14.920
As you wish.

14:16.150 --> 14:18.220
<i>I won't fall for that trick.</i>

14:18.220 --> 14:20.500
<i>I've got more experience.</i>

14:20.500 --> 14:22.770
It's probably just in her socks.

14:22.770 --> 14:25.090
That's a standard place kids hide stuff.

14:27.660 --> 14:30.290
That failed, too? Damn.

14:31.310 --> 14:33.140
I told you I don't have anything.

14:33.140 --> 14:36.960
Snot-nosed brat! I'll sell 
you to a slaver and then—

14:40.450 --> 14:43.150
Is it fun to pick on such a small girl?

14:43.150 --> 14:45.580
L-Lynsha. No, it's just...

14:45.580 --> 14:48.740
I thought we could get 
something worth some money.

14:49.130 --> 14:52.310
Jem's order was to bring 
the girl to him, right?

14:52.310 --> 14:54.240
Go make the arrangements at once.

14:54.240 --> 14:55.940
Wh-What arrangements?

14:56.340 --> 14:59.090
Don't tell me you were going to carry her.

14:59.090 --> 15:01.920
The revolutionaries should have 
a carriage we can use freely.

15:01.920 --> 15:04.130
<i>R-Revolutionaries?</i>

15:04.130 --> 15:07.350
And see how things are going 
for the operation, too!

15:07.350 --> 15:09.270
<i>O-Operation?</i>

15:09.270 --> 15:10.830
Okay.

15:14.060 --> 15:17.500
Now then, who are you exactly?

15:18.720 --> 15:21.820
<i>I might be in a pretty 
dicey situation right now.</i>

15:21.820 --> 15:24.750
<i>They said something about 
slavers just now, after all.</i>

15:24.750 --> 15:26.070
You don't want to say?

15:26.070 --> 15:28.220
Well, fine by me.

15:30.850 --> 15:32.840
Help me—

15:37.370 --> 15:40.370
Tell me. Can you stop this revolution?

15:41.370 --> 15:45.960
If you can, then please,
 save my brother.

15:46.220 --> 15:48.040
Stop the revolution?

15:48.040 --> 15:49.840
Save your brother?

15:49.840 --> 15:51.550
What do you mean?

15:51.830 --> 15:54.040
There's no time. We'll talk as we go.

15:54.040 --> 15:55.140
Put on your shoes.

15:58.140 --> 15:59.100
Where are we?

15:59.100 --> 16:01.810
One of the underground 
revolutionaries' bases.

16:01.810 --> 16:05.730
Stay close to me. It isn't safe here.

16:06.080 --> 16:10.470
Are the revolutionaries you mentioned the 
people who are causing the rebellion?

16:10.850 --> 16:15.100
Yes. You see, my brother is 
leading the revolutionaries.

16:15.950 --> 16:19.830
Your brother is the leader of 
the revolutionary organization?

16:19.830 --> 16:23.480
I may call them revolutionaries, 
but they're just a bunch of whiners.

16:24.000 --> 16:27.030
That blasted Jem is manipulating everyone.

16:27.450 --> 16:32.390
Why are you giving me inside 
information about the revolutionaries?

16:32.390 --> 16:34.710
Because of what Jem said.

16:34.710 --> 16:38.140
He told us to capture you because 
you pose a threat to the organization.

16:38.140 --> 16:39.150
Jem?

16:40.050 --> 16:41.580
In other words,

16:41.580 --> 16:46.040
you must have the power to stop the 
revolution and disband the revolutionaries.

16:48.640 --> 16:52.650
What could a child like me possibly do?

16:52.650 --> 16:57.360
Oh? You seemed pretty calm when those 
boys were threatening you earlier.

16:57.360 --> 16:59.940
And you seem awfully calm right now.

16:59.940 --> 17:01.990
I can't imagine you're just some child.

17:03.130 --> 17:04.250
Lynsha! No fair!

17:04.250 --> 17:07.250
You were trying to hog all 
the credit for yourself?

17:07.820 --> 17:09.320
You've made the arrangements already?

17:09.320 --> 17:11.500
N-No... you see...

17:11.500 --> 17:13.100
Thanks for the directions.

17:13.100 --> 17:15.550
Sorry. I had a slightly 
hard time finding you.

17:15.550 --> 17:17.120
Sion!

17:17.520 --> 17:19.000
Are you unharmed, Mia?

17:19.000 --> 17:20.430
Y-Yes.

17:20.430 --> 17:23.210
And who are you there, miss?

17:23.540 --> 17:24.590
I, uh...

17:24.590 --> 17:28.360
Her name is Lynsha. She's part of the 
underground revolutionary organization,

17:28.360 --> 17:30.570
but she saved me.

17:30.570 --> 17:33.860
She also shared information with me.

17:33.860 --> 17:38.160
How did you go from being held captive to
 making an ally of a revolutionary so quickly?

17:38.420 --> 17:42.150
<i>Don't tell me she got kidnapped on 
purpose in order to gain information...</i>

17:42.150 --> 17:43.230
<i>She did not.</i>

17:43.230 --> 17:46.120
We can consider each other allies, right?

17:46.120 --> 17:48.730
If you'll stop the revolution.

17:48.730 --> 17:50.850
Stop the revolution, eh?

17:50.850 --> 17:53.950
We'll have to get King Remno to do 
something about the heavy taxes...

17:54.260 --> 17:58.500
No, what my brother and the others are 
calling for is not a lowering of the taxes.

17:59.450 --> 18:04.000
They're calling for Lord Dasayev Donovan 
to be released from royal imprisonment.

18:04.300 --> 18:06.230
What do you mean?

18:06.230 --> 18:10.080
Apparently, in order to keep his 
chancellor, Lord Donovan, quiet,

18:10.080 --> 18:12.110
His Majesty has confined him somewhere.

18:12.420 --> 18:17.180
Did he not know what would happen if he 
harmed someone who spoke for the people?

18:17.450 --> 18:18.480
How foolish.

18:21.100 --> 18:24.110
Outland Count Rudolvon 
was the people's savior,

18:24.110 --> 18:28.290
supplying them with food after the nobles 
and the royal house abandoned them.

18:28.540 --> 18:32.200
It's obvious what consequences 
killing him would invite.

18:33.020 --> 18:37.120
Did you people fail to consider 
even something that simple?

18:37.740 --> 18:42.470
<i>At the time, Sion looked so self-satisfied. 
I wanted to tell him off.</i>

18:42.470 --> 18:45.140
<i>To tell him the very idea of 
that story was ridiculous.</i>

18:45.550 --> 18:50.720
<i>To tell him my father would never execute 
a vassal in order to maintain popularity.</i>

18:51.730 --> 18:55.680
There's something kind of 
strange about that story.

18:55.950 --> 18:57.720
W-We've got a problem!

19:02.880 --> 19:05.620
What's going on? What's all this commotion?

19:05.620 --> 19:09.960
W-Well, our comrades have risen up 
and are heading to the mayor's manor.

19:10.270 --> 19:13.430
What gives? I thought the 
operation was two days from now.

19:13.430 --> 19:14.920
Did Jem order it?

19:15.210 --> 19:17.880
No, your brother made the 
decision independently.

19:17.880 --> 19:21.330
He said it was to help our comrades 
who are confronting the army.

19:21.330 --> 19:23.180
Ugh, really?!

19:24.640 --> 19:26.940
Let's go to the mayor's manor!

19:29.010 --> 19:33.800
<i>She's got it in her head that </i>I'd<i> go 
to such a dangerous-seeming place?</i>

19:33.800 --> 19:37.220
Good grief. I think that'd 
be fairly dangerous.

19:37.220 --> 19:39.220
<i>Quite right.</i>

19:39.680 --> 19:41.950
But if you insist on going, I'll go with you.

19:41.950 --> 19:46.160
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Nobody's said we wanna go!

19:46.430 --> 19:48.950
I'd really like to rendezvous with Keithwood,

19:48.950 --> 19:51.030
but we can't pass up this 
opportunity you've created, Mia!

19:51.030 --> 19:53.130
<i>No, you've got it all wrong!</i>

19:53.130 --> 19:55.510
Off we go, then. Let's hurry.

19:59.030 --> 20:01.540
By the way, who's this "Jem"?

20:01.540 --> 20:03.200
A comrade of the revolutionary army.

20:03.200 --> 20:05.570
My brother said he met him at a bar.

20:05.570 --> 20:07.930
He's the one who said to kidnap Mia?

20:07.930 --> 20:10.630
Yes. He said she'd be an 
obstacle to the revolution.

20:10.910 --> 20:13.590
It's possible he's allied with the 
group that attacked our carriage.

20:18.470 --> 20:22.720
The river we fell into yesterday 
passes near here, doesn't it?

20:22.720 --> 20:26.520
It appears so. So this is an important 
spot for traffic of information...

20:26.520 --> 20:29.670
Could it be that it was this Jem guy

20:29.670 --> 20:32.040
that chose this town as the 
stage for the uprising?

20:32.040 --> 20:36.170
If so, then I get the distinct sense he's 
choosing places to attack precisely.

20:38.340 --> 20:40.270
What are those blue hoods?

20:40.270 --> 20:42.770
They're like a symbol of the revolutionaries.

20:42.770 --> 20:45.230
They're calling themselves 
the Blue Caps or something.

20:45.230 --> 20:47.030
The Blue Caps?

20:47.030 --> 20:49.930
That's perfect for us. 
Let's blend in with them.

20:51.310 --> 20:54.520
We're only making reasonable demands.

20:54.870 --> 20:58.090
We wish to make our suffering 
under the heavy taxes heard.

20:58.090 --> 21:02.470
We want Chancellor Dasayev, 
who spoke on our behalf, returned to us!

21:02.470 --> 21:05.950
But the royal government 
lends no ear to our voices!

21:06.590 --> 21:10.020
And the mayor has irresponsibly 
fled from this manor!

21:10.390 --> 21:15.750
It is a shame we couldn't prevent that, 
but we have safely taken the town.

21:15.750 --> 21:18.420
This is thanks to all of you, my comrades.

21:18.420 --> 21:20.220
Thank you, everyone.

21:21.630 --> 21:23.870
An agitator...

21:23.870 --> 21:26.260
His oratory is superb to win
 over the populace like this.

21:27.960 --> 21:30.310
Oh, Lynsha, you're here.

21:31.800 --> 21:33.420
Lambert...

21:33.420 --> 21:36.080
Oh? And who are those kids with you?

21:36.630 --> 21:39.480
Would they be the ones Jem mentioned?

21:39.800 --> 21:42.960
The ones with the potential 
to obstruct the revolution?

21:47.860 --> 21:49.260
Stop!

21:49.260 --> 21:51.890
If we turn our blades on young children,

21:51.890 --> 21:54.330
no one will listen to what 
we have to say anymore.

21:54.670 --> 21:57.960
Please, Lambert. Hear what 
these kids have to say!

21:58.850 --> 22:01.240
Hear what they have to say?

23:34.970 --> 23:39.980
Illustration by:
